{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n ':contract|contract ' test/yin/vm/debruijn_stack_test.cljc src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/stack.cljc | head -25; tail -20 collab/1791850000000-5a-first-numbers.log; rg -n 'contract' src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_code.cljc | head; sed -n '135,155p' src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/stack.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"rg: test/yin/vm/debruijn_stack_test.cljc: No such file or directory (os error 2)\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/stack.cljc:132:    (vm/check-contract! vm/stack-contract contract)\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/stack.cljc:149:   (`:contract-missing`, `:contract-mismatch`); the image must then pass\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/stack.cljc:381:   `:contract`, the segment's stamp, required when `segment` is non-empty\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/stack.cljc:438:         (load-image segment (:contract opts))\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/stack.cljc:954:  (link-format [_] {:format format-tag, :contract vm/stack-contract})\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/stack.cljc:972:                :contract vm/stack-contract}))\nLoading initial Timbre config from: :default\n\nRunning tests in #{\"test\"}\nWARNING: load already refers to: #'clojure.core/load in namespace: yin.vm.encoder, being replaced by: #'yin.vm.encoder/load\nSyntax error compiling at (yin/vm/semantic_register/derive_test.cljc:145:38).\nNo such var: vm/debruijn-contract\n\nFull report at:\n/var/folders/n0/xl3_1xkn0yd5trpq843l81840000gn/T/clojure-6761787217034114794.edn\n109:(def lowering-contract-version\n113:   `\\\"b2\\\"` contract, `yin.vm/stack-contract`): Rule R's `:define`.\"\n119:   contract version, arity (the opcode table's own mnemonic count), the\n122:   exported here as a documented contract point only. The morphism's\n129:   fork every image's H even though `lowering-contract-version` already\n133:  [[:yin.debruijn.code/dimension :dim/lowering-contract-version lowering-contract-version]\n553:   descriptor hash (which already folds in the lowering-contract\n                      defect)))))\n\n\n(defn load-image\n  \"Load `segment` (a vector of instructions) into `vm` as its one image:\n   H is recomputed, the registers are reset to pc 0 with empty frames,\n   stack, and continuation, and the machine is running unless the segment\n   is empty. The store, the parked map, the wait set, the ready queue,\n   the id counter, and the composition values survive, exactly as they\n   survive a `yin.vm.semantic/load-vector`. The offset table restarts at\n   `[H 0 n]`, so a continuation parked under an earlier image names no row\n   of it and `stack-restore` refuses it.\n\n   `contract` is required and compared with `vm/stack-contract` first\n   (`:contract-missing`, `:contract-mismatch`); the image must then pass\n   `yin.vm.debruijn-code/image-defect`, Rule R included. An empty segment\n   admits no code and needs neither.\"\n  [vm segment contract]\n  (admit! segment contract)\n  (install-image vm segment))\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
